| 3.2 | petcore seams: `holdMic func(bool)` on `core` (set to `audio.HoldMic` in `jni.go` init beside `stopDevices`), `State() voice.State` on the `engine` interface, `Lease() func()` on the `hostLink` interface; `applyTake()` under `c.mu`: `want := background && eng != nil && eng.State()==StateListening`; on change call `holdMic(want)` and log `android: microphone kept for the take` / `released`; take a lease when `want` turns true, release it when the app is foreground or the state is idle/error/offline. `SetForeground(false)` calls `applyTake()` **before** `stopDevices()`; `SetForeground(true)` calls it after `startDevices()`; `pump` calls it on every `voice.StateChanged` | `client/cmd/petcore/core.go`, `client/cmd/petcore/jni.go` | 2 | pending |

