# M07: End to end on the emulator and docs

## Tasks

A real app on the emulator records through a screen-off, sends the whole take on return, and the docs, changelog and CLAUDE.md describe the new behaviour.

**Scope** — `tools/android/e2e.sh`, `Justfile` (`android-e2e` doc comment only), `docs/android.md`, new `docs/decisions/0037-takes-survive-the-screen.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `CLAUDE.md`.

| Task | Description | Files | SP | Status |
|------|-------------|-------|----|--------|
| 7.1 | `MODE=screenoff` in `e2e.sh`: after «ui: chat ready», tap the talk button once (tap take), wait for `voice: tap take starts`, assert `dumpsys window` shows `KEEP_SCREEN_ON` for the app window and `dumpsys activity services dev.hermespet` lists `TakeService` as foreground; `input keyevent KEYCODE_SLEEP`; assert logcat `android: foreground false` and `android: microphone kept for the take` and **no** `audio: aaudio input closed while the devices are stopped` before the take ends; wait 8 s; `KEYCODE_WAKEUP`, `wm dismiss-keyguard`, tap again; assert `voice: take sent N ms` with N ≥ 8000, then request.start → transcript → `turn.end` as the ptt mode does; ends «android-e2e screenoff: ok»; update the mode list in the header comment and the `Justfile` recipe comment | `tools/android/e2e.sh`, `Justfile` | 2 | pending |
| 7.2 | Docs: `docs/android.md` new «Voice takes» section (5-min cap and `take_limit`, keep-screen-on, `TakeService`, mic hold and lease, the strip, system cancel → lock); ADR 0037 (context, decision, consequences: the Brick's hold cap rises to 5 min); `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]`: **Android:** bullets for the strip, screen-on and screen-off survival, an untagged bullet for the 5-min cap; `CLAUDE.md` rows below | `docs/android.md`, `docs/decisions/0037-takes-survive-the-screen.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `CLAUDE.md` | 1 | pending |

